L420: The models we fine-tuned were also re-prompted them with the Explicit Bias prompting technique. This would give us some concrete evidence on the resiliency of the models and stubbornness in un-learning bias. We can see here from cite112†Table 5.6 that GPT 3.5 was able to pick the stereotype correctly more often as compared to its base model. Notice with experiment, the proportion stayed around 75% with StereoSet increasing by 10% and CrowSPairs by 40%.
L421: There was not much success in the models performing better than these numbers. In this way, we can see that with such fine-tuning we can train models to be able to identify the stereotype better so that it can avoid such stereotype when prompted implicitly.
